<title>UK: UK's Clarke says stg to have deflationary impact.</title>
<headline>UK's Clarke says stg to have deflationary impact.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said on Wednesday the pound's appreciation would have a deflationary effect on the economy.</p>
<p>&quot;Sterling is going to have a big deflationary effect,&quot; he told BBC radio in an interview.</p>
<p>The pound has appreciated 14 percent on a trade weighted basis since August last year.</p>
<p>-- Rosemary Bennett +44 171 542 7715</p>
